[{"name":"Release v1.15.0","uuid":"344880880","tag_name":"v1.15.0","target_commitish":"main","body":"\r\nWelcome to the v1.15.0 release of Kit! This release improves support for the CNCF ModelPack format, adds support for more options when packing ModelKit data, and adds support for MCP bundles.\r\n\r\n## New Features\r\n\r\n### Improved CNCF ModelPack support\r\nKit is now better at handling [CNCF ModelPack](https://github.com/modelpack/model-spec/blob/main/docs/spec.md) artifacts. When working with a ModelPack that was not generated by Kit, Kit can interpret the fields normally found within a Kitfile from the ModelPack's configuration and annotations.\r\n\r\nTo use Kit to package artifacts in the ModelPack format instead of ModelKit, you can use the flag `--use-model-pack` for the `pack` command. Note that not all KitOps features are supported by ModelPacks currently.\r\n\r\nUltimately, you should be able to use ModelPacks with KitOps, regardless of how they were created. For example, the Docker CLI recently added support for creating ModelPacks, and those are now compatible with KitOps.\r\n\r\nFor more details, see [PR #1202](https://github.com/kitops-ml/kitops/pull/1202)\r\n\r\n### Additional format and compression options for artifact layers\r\n\r\nBy default, Kit packages each _layer_ (model weights, datasets, code, etc.) as an uncompressed tarball, which provides a good tradeoff in terms of usability, size, and speed. With KitOps v1.15.0, the following extra options are now available while packing ModelKits (or ModelPacks)\r\n\r\n* Compression options: in addition to the existing `--compression=gzip` option, KitOps now supports using Zstandard compression via the flag `--compression=zstd`. \r\n* Layer format options: instead of packaging files and/or directories as tarballs, Kit can now package _single_ files as-is -- i.e. with no tar wrapper. The primary benefit of the raw format is that the layer DiffID (and digest, for the no compression case) match the actual SHA256 sum of the file on disk, making it easier to track which files are stored in which ModelKits.\r\n\r\n   To enable raw layers, use the flag `--layer-format=raw` on the pack command, though note that this flag currently applies to all layers in the Kitfile.\r\n\r\nThese changes were added as part of improving ModelPack support; for more information, see [PR #1202](https://github.com/kitops-ml/kitops/pull/1202) \r\n\r\n### MCP support in ModelKits\r\nWith Kit v1.15.0, the Kitfile now has a `mcpServers` section, which can be used to package MCP bundles (`.mcpb`) files in a new layer format. These bundles are a common way to distribute MCP servers, and adding them to the Kitfile allows for building automation and management around MCP servers specifically.\r\n\r\nFor more details on how MCP bundles are handled, see [PR #1214](https://github.com/kitops-ml/kitops/pull/1214)\r\n\r\n## Bug Fixes\r\n* Improve auth header handling for push operations by @amisevsk in https://github.com/kitops-ml/kitops/pull/1194\r\n* Respect KITOPS_HOME in library config path by @puneetdixit200 in https://github.com/kitops-ml/kitops/pull/1189\r\n* Add image manifest mediatype to manifests created by Kit by @amisevsk in https://github.com/kitops-ml/kitops/pull/1218\r\n* fix: tolerate missing content in local list and remove by @gorkem in https://github.com/kitops-ml/kitops/pull/1217\r\n\r\n## New Contributors\r\n* @puneetdixit200 made their first contribution in https://github.com/kitops-ml/kitops/pull/1189\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/kitops-ml/kitops/compare/v1.14.0...v1.15.0\r\n\r\n","draft":false,"prerelease":false,"immutable":false,"published_at":"2026-06-25T17:34:11.000Z","created_at":"2026-06-25T20:03:16.354Z","author":"github-actions[bot]","assets":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kitops-ml/kitops/releases/assets/457851830","id":457851830,"node_id":"RA_kwDOLNJZqs4bSkO2","name":"kitops-darwin-arm64.tar.gz","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bo